# i18n Rules (next-intl, no locale routing)

The app is bilingual Arabic (RTL, default) / English (LTR). Locale comes from the `NEXT_LOCALE` cookie + `User.locale` — URLs never contain a locale segment. Config lives in `src/i18n/`; messages in `messages/ar.json` + `messages/en.json` (namespaced per module: `common`, `trucks`, `contracts`, ...).

## UI Text

- NEVER hardcode user-facing strings (Arabic or English) in components. Add a key to **BOTH** `messages/ar.json` and `messages/en.json`, then:
  - Client components: `const t = useTranslations("namespace")` → `t("key")`
  - Server components / route handlers: `const t = await getTranslations("namespace")`
- A key present in one messages file but missing in the other is a bug.
- Legacy modules still contain hardcoded Arabic (migrated module-by-module per the bilingual i18n plan). When touching a legacy file for other reasons, don't mass-migrate it — but any NEW string you add must use message keys.

## Layout & Direction

- NEVER hardcode `dir="rtl"`, `side="right"`, or assume RTL. Derive from locale: `getTextDirection(locale)` from `@/i18n/config`.
- Use logical CSS only: `ms-/me-/ps-/pe-/start-/end-/text-start/text-end` — never `ml-/mr-/pl-/pr-/left-/right-/text-left/text-right` (except for direction-independent values like `.financial-value` / `.weight-value`, which stay LTR).
- Components that portal outside the root (Sheet, Dialog, dropdowns) must receive `dir` explicitly.

## Numbers & Dates

- Numbers/amounts/weights: helpers in `src/lib/number-format.ts` (Latin digits in both languages). Dates: `src/lib/date-format.ts`. NEVER call `toLocaleString("ar-EG" | "ar-SA" | "en-US")` directly in components.

## Reference Data & Server Messages

- Localized DB fields shipped in phase 5: `Destination.nameEn`, `SizeLookup.displayNameEn`, `Role.displayNameEn`, `Permission.displayNameEn`, plus optional `StockYard.nameEn` / `StockLocation.nameEn`. All are nullable and fall back to the Arabic column.
  - Display with the helpers in `src/lib/localized-name.ts`: `localizedDestination`, `localizedSize`, `localizedRole`, `localizedPermission`, `localizedStockName`, or the generic `localizedName(entity, locale, { arField, enField })` / `pickLocalizedName(locale, ar, en)`.
  - Prefer localizing at the API/service boundary (get the locale via `getRequestLocale()` in Node route handlers) so the existing `name`/`displayName` field already carries the right language — see `/api/destinations`, `/api/sizes`, `/api/admin/roles`, and the user-permission matrix service (which takes an optional `locale`).
  - The English seed values for destinations/sizes mirror `src/lib/en-labels.ts`; roles/permissions carry `displayNameEn` in `prisma/rbac-source.ts` and are synced by `scripts/sync-rbac.ts` (`npm run rbac:sync:dry` before `rbac:sync`).
  - Still Arabic-only for now (gradual migration): destination/size names embedded in truck / scale / stock / billet list responses, the report exports (which keep `en-labels.ts` as a documented fallback), and `session.roleName` baked into the JWT at login.
- `ServiceError` / Zod messages use translation keys (phase 4) resolved at the API/middleware boundary. To include an enum value in a message, pass an enum-reference param like `@enums.materialKind.REBAR` (or `@enums.contractStatus.active`); `resolveEnumRefs` in `src/lib/i18n/server-messages.ts` translates it to the request locale. Never pass raw Arabic label strings as params.

## Rollout Guard

- The language switcher is dark-launched behind `LANGUAGE_SWITCHER_ENABLED` (see `src/config/feature-flags.ts`). Do NOT render it unconditionally or remove the flag until the i18n plan's phase 7 (full translation coverage).
